\path (2.1,0.4) node[black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont] {$\dot{x}(0)=9\sqrt{3}$};
\path (4.5,-1.2) node[right,black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont] {$\dot{y}(0)=-9$};
\path (1.35,-0.32) node[black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont] {$30^{\circ}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Integrate $\underset{\sim}{a}=-9.8\underset{\sim}{j}$:
$\underset{\sim}{v}=C_{1}\underset{\sim}{i}+(-9.8t+C_{2})\underset{\sim}{j}$.

At $t=0$,
$\begin{align*}C_{1}&=9\sqrt{3}\\C_{2}&=-9.\end{align*}$

Therefore,
$\underset{\sim}{v}(t)=9\sqrt{3}\underset{\sim}{i}-(9+9.8t)\underset{\sim}{j}\text{ m/s}$.

Since $\theta$ is acute and $\tan\theta=\dfrac{4}{3}$,
$\cos\theta=\dfrac{3}{5}$ and $\sin\theta=\dfrac{4}{5}$.

The initial conditions are
$\begin{align*}\underset{\sim}{v}(0)&=45\left(\dfrac{3}{5}\right)\underset{\sim}{i}+45\left(\dfrac{4}{5}\right)\underset{\sim}{j}\\&=27\underset{\sim}{i}+36\underset{\sim}{j}\\\underset{\sim}{r}(0)&=18\underset{\sim}{j}.\end{align*}$

